      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "1. To find out how much the painting costs in US dollars, we need to convert the amount from Namibian dollars to US dollars.\n2. Since we know the exchange rate of 1 US dollar = 7 Namibian dollars, we can calculate the number of US dollars needed to reach 105 Namibian dollars.\n3. Divide the amount in Namibian dollars (105) by the exchange rate (7) to find the equivalent amount in US dollars.\n4. US dollars = Namibian dollars / Exchange rate\n5. So, 105 Namibian dollars / 7 Namibian dollars per US dollar = 15 US dollars\n6. The painting would then cost 15 US dollars in USD.\n7. Now that we have the price in USD, we need to find out how much it costs in Chinese yuan.\n8. Since 1 US dollar = 6 Chinese yuan, we can calculate the number of Chinese yuan needed to reach 15 US dollars.\n9. Divide the amount in US dollars (15) by the exchange rate (6) to find the equivalent amount in Chinese yuan.\n10. Chinese yuan = US dollars / Exchange rate\n11. So, 15 US dollars / 6 US dollars per Chinese yuan = 2.5 Chinese yuan\n12. Therefore, the painting would cost 2.5 Chinese yuan in Chinese yuan.\nYou are an AI assistant. User will you give you a task. Your goal is to complete the task as faithfully as you can. While performing the task think step-by-step and justify your steps.",
